In my early Nethack era - not knowing better - I even wished for
blessed potions of gain level for the abilities. But they are not
worth a wish; there are many more important items to wish for.

Nonetheless I find the abilities very important. In the early game
Str for the carrying capacity, later for the damage bonus. I find
Con to be extremely useful early for regeneration, and I think it
also gives a HP bonus on XL gain (but I'm not sure about the latter).
Int is, as you say, good for spell casters; but primarily not for
casting spells - some roles even do require Wis for that - but for
learning spells. I had a few good clerical roles that could well
cast spells but did have lousy Int to learn the spells in the first
place. Dex is good for placing a hit. Only Cha is a property that I
don't find overly useful.

To sum up; most abilities are very useful and should be fostered.

